16.
Business to be transacted by special resolution.
- The following class of business shall be transacted by a special resolution alone-
(i)
all matters in respect of which the obligation to transact the business by special resolution has been specifically laid
down in the Act or any rule made thereunder;
(ii)
delegation or resumption of any power or function under Section 34;
(iii)
agreeing to take over any new function delegated under Section 34;
(iv)
consideration of and approving the draft Plan of the Khand under Section 86;
(v)
appointment of committees under Section 87 (1) and (2);
(vi)
making investment under Section 101 (3);
(vii)
transfer of property under Section 107;
(viii)
